WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.369
-My first guest hosts
a brand-new competition series

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.304
called "Crime Scene Kitchen,"

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:09.542
which premieres Wednesday,
May 26th at 9:00 p.m. on Fox.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.712
Here is Joel McHale!

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.781
Oh.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.182
Oh, my -- Oh, wow.

00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:19.819
Oh! Wow. Unbelievable.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.020
Oh, wow, wow.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.254
Oh, welcome.
-Thank you.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:23.556
-Joel, wow.
-Thank you.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.924
-Wow! Oh, my --

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.493
-Thank you. Oh, man.
-Joel. Oh, my goodness.

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.028
Joel, welcome. Welcome.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.496
-[ Sighs ]
-Oh! There's a --

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.464
-Oh!
-Oh!

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:34.266
Oh, my goodness.
It's a pet of --

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:36.502
Joel, thank you so much.
What an entrance.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:37.536
Who is that?
-Yeah.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:39.605
-Who is that friend?
-I don't know.

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.674
-[ Laughs ] Oh, my gosh.
They didn't make --

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.676
-I just know
it's going to be way better

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.545
than that cat that doesn't
really play piano.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:50.549
-[ Laughs ]
I thought it was perfect.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:51.851
-Oh.
-Hey, get a --

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.387
See, Joel, this is --
Oh, my God.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.890
Joel? Joel, be careful, Joel.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.424
Be careful, now.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:00:59.658
[ Imitates spitting ]
-Okay.

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:01.094
[ Laughs ]

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.162
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.899
Joel, we love you, buddy.
Welcome.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.901
-Oh, oh, wait for the click.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.269
Ahh. There it is.
-Alright.

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:13.572
Buddy, I follow you
on social media, and --

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:14.574
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.777
Well, Jimmy, let me tell ya --

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.779
I actually didn't freeze.
I just made that up.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:23.016
-I know you did.
Joel, I thought, I thought --

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.251
You're not frozen, Joel.
Your eyes are moving, Joel.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.719
-Oh, sorry. Sorry, okay.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.388
-I follow you on social media,
and I want to ask you a question

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:33.526
'cause you do a lot of grilling
and, like, smoking.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.629
You do like 11-hour
smoking things.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.932
I'm going head-to-head
with Tariq soon from The Roots.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:42.001
We're having
a barbecue-off competition.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.402
I'm trying to decide
what to make.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:46.672
-Oh. You're dead meat.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.074
You've already lost.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.143
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.278
-Are you talking about
what's on the grill,

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.513
or are you talking about --

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.848
-Life? No.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.249
Uh, you're winning.

00:01:57.249 --> 00:02:00.386
No. Okay. So, you're going
to go up against Tariq,

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.822
and you need to out-grill him,
right?

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.490
-That's correct.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:09.028
-Okay. Tariq, can I give you
a recipe to make?

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.930
'Cause I do cook a lot of meat,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.533
'cause I was like, if the virus
isn't going to get me,

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:15.033
I'm going to die
of high cholesterol.

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:16.702
-That's very smart, Joel.

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:19.872
Now -- But, yeah, Tariq, can you
--

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.807
Can you earmuff? Can you just,
like, plug your ears?

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.375
-Can you earmuff?
-I mean, doesn't matter.

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:25.244
You can --
Give him your recipe, I guess.

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.213
I don't -- You know, cool.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.014
-Okay, here it is.

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:31.684
Jimmy, do you cook at all?

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.452
-Yes, absolutely. Anything --
-Okay, good.

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:37.123
-Yeah, anything
in the microwave, absolutely.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:39.492
-Alright, great. This is good.
You want to take a steak

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.794
and just stick it
in the microwave for 35 minutes.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:42.795
It'll be fine.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.163
-[ Laughs ] Perfect.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.332
No, I do some cooking.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.168
-Okay, well, then, have you
heard of the brown butter method

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.270
for a bone-in rib eye?

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.538
-No.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.340
-Oh.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.243
And have you heard of a comb?

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.912
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:02.014
-I'm looking into the comb.
I'm looking into the comb.

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:03.382
Sorry, we're getting to that.

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:05.084
-I'll never be as cute as you,

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.853
but I want to give you this
recipe,

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.854
and you will beat Tariq with it,
I swear.

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:11.724
-Wow. There you go.
Do you hear that right there?

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:15.361
-Hello? Hello, B-Bobby Flay?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.731
Yeah, man, I'm gonna need you to
do that thing we talked about.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.265
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my gosh.

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:22.068
-Okay.
-Did you say Bobby Flay

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.137
or Bobby Fillet?
-Sorry?

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.172
-Did you say Bobby Flay
or Bobby Fillet?

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.041
-I didn't say anything.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.575
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:32.512
-I have an idea, and I think
I'm going to win this one.

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:35.882
What is some of the craziest
stuff you've ever eaten?

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.650
I know you're a big foodie.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.120
-Well, I had
lamb's brain pasta one time.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.522
Um, that was for my wedding.

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:46.292
And then --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.027
-You can have that
or the lasagna.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.628
Yeah, lamb brains pasta.

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:51.264
-Uh...
-I'll go with the fish.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.564
-The cake -- No.

00:03:52.564 --> 00:03:55.368
But I've had cobra before.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:59.872
-Maybe I could grill a cobra.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.474
-Well, I've never done that,

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:06.179
and I assume "Rikki-Tikki-Tavi"
fans will be very upset.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:07.646
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:09.882
-Wow. Deep cut, deep cut.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.185
You got Questlove --
-That's for everybody over 50!

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.820
-You got Questlove
with that one.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.854
-Hey!

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:16.489
-What? You did.
-Yeah.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:17.523
You were laughing.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.058
-Okay, yes, I was.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.626
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:22.195
He's like, "Eh."

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:24.197
-Joel, I want to ask you
about a couple things,

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:28.334
'cause we usually talk about
whatever your next project is,

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.836
and most recently,
it was "Card Sharks."

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:32.272
You're the host
of "Card Sharks."

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:34.440
It's returning,
so congrats on that.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.808
-Yeah. We have actual --

00:04:36.808 --> 00:04:38.945
actual shark contestants
this year.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.446
So it's exciting.
-That's not true, again. No.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.716
June 16th, 10:00 p.m. on ABC.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.050
And that's all well and good,

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.952
but then you go, "No,
I want to take it a step up,"

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.388
and this is what I want
to talk to you about.

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.521
I'm very interested in this.

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:51.924
It's called
"Crime Scene Kitchen."

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.159
This is on Fox.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.194
-Now, explain
what the show is to me.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.595
It's not a crime scene, right?

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:58.531
-No, no, you go
to a crime scene,

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.367
and then you eat
next to a murder victim.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.868
-No, that's not true. No, no.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.736
-It's terrifying.

00:05:04.736 --> 00:05:08.907
No. Okay, it's crime scene
in that there's a kitchen,

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:13.012
and something was baked there,
some sort of wonderful dessert.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:17.350
Skilled bakers, some trained,
some not trained, go in there,

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.552
and they just find tiny,
little pieces of evidence

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:23.422
like a drop of lemon
or a little bit of frosting,

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:27.860
and then they are like, "I got
it. It's a hummingbird cake,"

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.529
and they have two hours
to try to recreate it.

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:36.068
So if you like baked goods and
the thrill of solving murders,

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:38.370
then you are in luck.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.539
-That's what I'm talking about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:42.442
That's a show for today.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.910
That's what I'm talking about.
-Yeah.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.211
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.479
Here is Joel McHale
in "Crime Scene Kitchen."

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:48.681
Take a look at this.

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:50.249
-I'm generally a very stoic

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:53.152
and put-together,
composed person.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.253
Ooh!

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.921
But I'm also very jumpy.

00:05:55.921 --> 00:05:57.223
I'm out of breath. This is --

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.925
-Hey, guys! What's going on?!
-Oh! Jesus Christ.

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:01.126
-How you doing?!

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:02.261
What's happening?

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:03.329
-Great. Really good.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.630
-Look at this!
-We're really good.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.098
-Are you here to distract us?

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.733
-Whoo! Yeah!

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:09.668
Look at all this. Okay.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:12.071
-This is really helpful.
Thank you.

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:14.607
I have a lot of work to do,
so get out of here.

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:17.509
-I'll find more ways to make fun
of your turtleneck later.

00:06:17.509 --> 00:06:20.679
-You know, I don't find myself
making fun of your outfit.

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:22.681
-No, but I'm
the host of the show.

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:25.384
-That's exactly right.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:26.819
You're doing what you should do.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:27.887
Joel McHale, everybody.

